    "answer_text": "A \u00a320,000 UFPLS for a Scottish member splits as: \u00a35,000 tax-free; \u00a315,000 taxed at your Scottish rates (emergency S-code on month 1, likely over-deducting). The payment triggers the \u00a310,000 Money Purchase Annual Allowance cap on future DC contributions, even on first draw. You cannot cancel or reverse the LSA/MPAA consequences, even if you return the money. Expect 5\u201310 business days for payment. You'll need to claim back excess emergency tax using P55 when fully complete, or Self Assessment.",
